"One hand has always been" two UHV projects put into operation
On the 26th, the quasi-east ± 1100 kV high-voltage DC transmission project and the Sutong 1000 kV AC UHV GIL integrated pipe gallery project were put into operation.
These two projects occupy the commanding heights of the current world's transmission technology in their respective fields, and after being put into operation, China's large-scale optimized allocation of energy will be greatly improved.
Guo Zhi, chief economist of the National Energy Administration, said that the Qiangdong to Wannan project is the world's largest power transmission capacity and the farthest transmission distance transmission project in the world.
Its operation is of great significance to promoting the development of Xinjiang's energy base and ensuring the power supply in eastern China.
GIL, i.e. gas-insulated metal closed transmission lines.
Sutong pipe gallery project has created the GIL project's record with the highest global voltage level and the strongest conveying capacity, and has realized the operation of the "AC double ring network" with the highest voltage level of the backbone power grid in East China.
According to the State Grid Corporation, the transmission distance of Qiandong to Wannan Project is 3,324 kilometers.
If conventional technology is used, more than 15% of the electrical energy will be lost on the way, and the project has been researched and developed to greatly increase the economic transmission distance to more than 3,000 kilometers.
After the operation of the Qiandong to Wannan project, 100 million degrees of electricity can be transported every 8 hours and 20 minutes, which can help solve the problem of the consumption of existing new energy in Xinjiang.
It is estimated that the annual power transmission of this single line will reach 60 to 85 billion kWh, which can meet more than half of Shanghai's electricity consumption throughout the year.
Sutong GIL Integrated Pipe Corridor Project is a control project of the UHV communication ring network spanning the Yangtze River.
If the conventional overhead line is used across the river, it is necessary to set up two giant towers of more than 450 meters on the Yangtze River, and to build an artificial island of more than four football fields for each tower.
In this regard, the national power grid bold innovation, the development of compact UHV AC GIL transmission technology, through the tunnel from underwater across the river, to avoid the impact on the golden channel.
The two projects have promoted China's electrical equipment manufacturing capacity to achieve a new leap forward.
At present, the national power grid has built a total of "10 to 11 straight" UHV project, as well as "4 to 3 straight" under construction.
Foreign Exchange Bureau: China's external debt structure continues to optimize the stability of foreign debt
"Overall, China's external debt structure continues to be optimized, and the stability of foreign debt is enhanced."
Wang Chunying, spokesman and chief economist of the State Administration of Foreign Exchange, said on the 27th that the main indicators of China's external debt are within the internationally recognized security line, and the external debt risk is generally controllable.
Wang Chunying made the above-mentioned statement in response to a reporter's question in response to the foreign exchange bureau's release of foreign debt data at the end of June 2019.
According to the data, as of the end of June 2019, China's full caliber (including foreign currency) external debt balance was 1998 billion US dollars, an increase of 26.3 billion US dollars from the end of March 2019, an increase of 1.3%, mainly due to the increase in the balance of debt securities.
In the second quarter of 2019, more than 70% of China's full-caliber external debt was driven by non-resident purchases of domestic RMB bonds, and non-residents were mainly dominated by medium- and long-term investors such as the central bank.
At the end of June 2019, the proportion of medium- and long-term foreign debt increased by 3 percentage points compared with the end of March 2019, and the foreign debt of local currencies increased by 1 percentage point compared with the end of March 2019.
Wang Chunying said that with the inclusion of China's domestic RMB bonds in April 2019 in the Bloomberg Barclays Global Comprehensive Index, international investors' recognition of China's bond market has been further enhanced, and domestic RMB bonds have been continuously increased.
"China's balance of payments to maintain an overall balance, external debt risk can be controlled."
The reporter learned from the Yunnan Provincial Academy of Agricultural Sciences on the 27th that at present, the nocturnal moth in Yunnan grassland has been effectively prevented and controlled, which has not caused a large-scale outbreak, and the prevention and control work has achieved phased results.
In January of this year, Jiangcheng County, Pu'er City, Yunnan Province, was found for the first time to move into a grassland nocturnal moth from abroad, which was subsequently confirmed in 129 counties in Yunnan, and the grassland nocturnal moth also gradually spread from Yunnan to mainland China, posing a direct threat to China's food production.
Grassland nocturnal moth is an important agricultural pest of multi-eating long-flying nature originating in tropical and subtropical regions of the Americas, and is a major migratory pest in the global early warning of the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations, which has the characteristics of "international, flying, explosive and destructive".
The pest endangers more than 80 kinds of crops such as corn, sugarcane, and sorghum, with a large amount of food intake, which can cause up to 70% of production losses.
It is difficult to prevent and control, and there are no registered pesticides to prevent and control the worm in China.
Since the relocation of grassland nocturnal moths into Yunnan, the Yunnan Provincial Academy of Agricultural Sciences has selected Chen Aidong as a researcher to lead the innovation team of agricultural cross-border pest prevention and control in the Yunnan Provincial Academy of Agricultural Sciences in cooperation with green prevention and control, going to the front line, conducting field surveys, collecting samples, and carrying out technical guidance and test demonstrations.
The team has initially grasped the population characteristics of the nocturnal moth in Yunnan grassland, natural enemy insect resources, the characteristics of overseas insect sources, the trajectory of population migration, the virulence of agents, and the effect of field prevention and control.
They actively carry out research and application of green prevention and control technology, through the implementation of new green prevention and control technologies such as population monitoring, adult booby trapping, scientific drugs and agronomic measures, the prevention and control effect in the demonstration area has reached more than 90%, while reducing the use of chemical pesticides, protecting natural enemy resources and the ecological environment, and providing technical support for Yunnan to effectively control the outbreak and sustainable management of grassland nocturnal moths.
At present, the nocturnal moth of Yunnan grassland has received effective prevention and control, which has not caused a large-scale outbreak, and the prevention and control work has achieved phased results.
In the next step, the Yunnan Provincial Academy of Agricultural Sciences will focus on carrying out the ecological mechanism of the outbreak of population relocation and flight, and break through the construction of biological prevention and control and green prevention and control technology system.
At the same time, we will actively promote cross-border international cooperation, and strive to establish joint key laboratories and joint monitoring outlets and demonstration areas abroad to enhance the full range of monitoring and early warning capabilities of Yunnan grassland nocturnal moths.
According to the website of the People's Bank of China, the People's Bank of China is scheduled to issue a set of panda gold and silver commemorative coins at the China International Import Expo on September 30, 2019.
There are a total of 2 gold and silver commemorative coins, including 1 gold commemorative coins and 1 silver commemorative coins, all of which are legal tender of the People's Republic of China.
According to reports, the set of gold and silver commemorative coins on the front of the pattern is the Beijing Temple of Heaven prayer hall, and publishes the national name, year number and "China International Import Expo" Chinese words.
8 grams of round gold commemorative coins on the back of the pattern for the mother and son panda map, and published "8g Au.999", "China International Import Expo" English words and denominations.
On the back of the 30-gram circular silver commemorative coin, the picture of the mother and sid panda, and the words "30g Ag.999", "China International Import Expo" have English words and denominations.
According to reports, 8 grams of circular gold commemorative coins for general currency, including pure gold 8 grams, diameter of 22 mm, denomination of 100 yuan, color 99.9%, the maximum circulation of 10,000 pieces.
30 grams of circular silver commemorative coins are general currency, including sterling silver 30 grams, diameter of 40 mm, denomination of 10 yuan, color 99.9%, the maximum circulation of 20,000 pieces.
This set of gold and silver commemorative coins was minted by Shenyang Mint Co., Ltd., the chief distribution of China Gold Coin Corporation.
White paper: China has embarked on a development path in line with national conditions
BEIJING, Sept. 27 (Xinhua) -- China's State Council Information Office released a white paper "China and the World in the New Era" on September 27.
The white paper pointed out that in the past 70 years, the Chinese people have explored and made great progress, successfully opened up the path of socialism with Chinese characteristics, and achieved remarkable development achievements.
According to the white paper, China's development depends on self-reliance and hard struggle.
China's development depends on the practical spirit of "800 million shirts for a Boeing", and the generations have worked hard and continued to work hard, giving others unimaginable hard work and sweat; relying on the spirit of "their own burden to carry themselves", regardless of prosperity or adversity, do not export problems, do not pass on contradictions, do not develop themselves by buying and selling, plundering other countries; relying on the exploration spirit of "touching the stone and crossing the river".
According to the white paper, China's development in the interaction with the world, China's development has injected positive energy into world peace and development, and China's road is in line with China's national conditions and adapting to the requirements of the times.
China has taken concrete actions to safeguard world peace.
In the past 70 years, China has not taken the initiative to provoke any war and conflict, and has not occupied an inch of land in other countries.
The white paper pointed out that in the past 70 years, China's development has achieved great success, and the fundamental reason is to find the correct development path of socialism with Chinese characteristics and unswervingly follow this path.
This is a path that is established from the perspective of national conditions, putting the interests of the people first, reforming and innovating, seeking common development in opening up, and adhering to the rule of law in an all-round way.
China's huge volume, complex national conditions, the difficulty of governance is rare in the world, there is no centralized unity, strong leadership, China will move towards division and disintegration, bringing disasters to the world.
In the past 70 years, China has overcome various risks and challenges, creating another remarkable Chinese miracle.
In particular, since the 18th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, China's development has made historic achievements and undergone historical changes, and the Chinese nation has ushered in a great leap from standing up and getting rich to getting stronger, closer to the great goal of national rejuvenation than at any time in history.
China's development path will show more and more bright development prospects with the advancement of the times.
Textile representatives from 45 countries and regions jointly issued the World Declaration.
On the 27th, at the 2019 2nd World Textile Merchants Conference held in Keqiao District of Shaoxing City, Zhejiang Province, representatives of the textile industry from 45 countries and regions jointly issued the "World Chamber of Commerce Declaration".
The declaration pointed out that facing the future, relevant countries adhere to open coordination, science and technology-driven, fashion change, and will work together to promote the high-quality development of the world's textile industry.
This year's World Textile Conference gathered about 1,200 representatives of the textile industry in 45 countries and regions, focusing on the trend of the textile industry in the world economic pattern and exploring the sustainable development of the global textile industry and the road of win-win cooperation.
Sun Ruizhe, president of the China Textile Industry Federation, said that the current global industrial division of labor pattern, trade pattern, innovation pattern have undergone profound adjustments, the textile industry has entered a new stage of globalization, innovation, responsible development, "science and technology, fashion, green" development concept is deepening.
Standing at the "crossroads" of global textile transformation and upgrading, Sun Ruizhe said, "To achieve sustainable development and common prosperity of the industry, it is necessary for the global textile people to actively participate, the leaders and the sharing of interests."
At the meeting, representatives of the textile circles of 45 countries and regions jointly issued the "World Chamber of Commerce Declaration" and jointly expounded on the development goals and vision of the global textile industry.
Facing the future, relevant countries will adhere to openness and coordination, continuously promote the interconnection of industries and markets, and jointly improve the development level of the industrial chain; they will adhere to the driving force of science and technology, continuously strengthen basic research, applied research and technology transformation, and jointly enhance the basic ability of the industry; they will concentrate on fashion and change, give full play to the role of textiles and clothing as cultural carriers and civilization bridges, and jointly enhance industrial cultural value.
Loureno Bartholomei, president of the Brazilian Fashion Designers Association, said in an interview that the release of the "World Business Declaration" will help various countries to jointly improve the development level of the textile industry chain and realize the sustainable development of the textile industry.
Loureno Bartholomei, for example, mentioned that there are more than 130 high-end local ready-to-wear brands in the Brazilian Fashion Designers Association, designers are committed to designing stylish, high-end ready-to-wear products, and Keqiao has a variety of boutique fabrics, "Through this cloth business conference, we also look forward to connecting with Keqiao's excellent suppliers and seeking more cooperation opportunities."
As the venue of the World Textile Conference, Keqiao has the world's largest textile market, and is gradually building a new pattern of upgrading and opening up to the outside world with its unique textile industry chain, representing China's textile image at the forefront of the world.
Shen Zhijiang, secretary of the Keqiao District Party Committee, said that Keqiao will take the opportunity of this cloth business conference to promote the textile industry in the direction of becoming more open, inclusive, inclusive, balanced and win-win.
Reuters estimates that the middle price of the yuan is expected to open around 7.0883 yuan, with a counter-cyclical impact of 460 points.
According to the RMB exchange rate formation mechanism published by the China Foreign Exchange Trading Center (CFETS), the middle price of the yuan against the U.S. dollar is expected to open around 7.0883 yuan on Friday, down about 154 points from the previous day.
In the previous day, the RMB immediately closed at 7.1315 yuan against the US dollar, while the median price was 7.0729 yuan.
According to the pricing mechanism, among today's middle price changes, there are 586 points that reflect the impact of market supply and demand, and another 27 points that reflect the number of points required for the overnight basket of exchange rates to remain basically unchanged; there are 460 points that reflect the impact of "counter-cyclical factors".
The median price of the yuan against the U.S. dollar in the previous day was estimated by Reuters at 7.0947 yuan, compared with 218 point deviations from the actual value announced by the foreign exchange trading center.
According to the middle price estimate published by CFETS, the RMB exchange rate CFETS index, the reference SDR (Special Drawing Rights) basket index and the reference BIS (Bank for International Settlements) basket index were 91.26, 91.46 and 94.92, respectively.
The completion of Tianjin, the first tallest building in northern China, has created more than 100 national patent achievements.
On the afternoon of the 26th, it was held in Tianjin Binhai New Area, marking the success of the collaborative management platform of the high-precision BIM model, a collaborative management platform in the field of skyscraper construction, which was independently developed by the project department of the Tianjin Chow Taifu Financial Center Project Department of the Eighth Bureau of China Construction, which won the Global Excellence Award in the Global Engineering and Construction Industry.
Located in the economic and technological development zone of Tianjin City, the Tianjin Chow Taifu Financial Center has a total construction area of 390,000 square meters, 4 floors underground, 100 floors above ground, and a construction height of 530 meters, covering Class A offices, luxury apartments, ultra-five star hotels, etc. After completion, it will become an important part of Tianjin's international landmark complex.
According to the relevant person in charge of the project department of the Tianjin Chow Taifu Financial Center of the Eighth Bureau, the total amount of steel used in the whole project is more than 70,000 tons, the high-altitude group is about 376,000 meters of welds, which is equivalent to the height of 42.5 Zhumulama Peaks, the use of weld wire can circle the earth 40 times, the number of steel components reaches 42,000 pieces, more than 50% are non-standard components.
The complexity and difficulty of the steel structure of the Tianjin Chow Taifu project is unprecedented.
According to industry insiders, the Tianjin Chow Taifu Financial Center has taken the lead in the all-round implementation of building information modeling (BIM) management in the skyscraper projects that have been built or built in the country.
The creative proposal and successful implementation of the "three full BIM applications" model of full participation, all-professional applications and the implementation of the whole process have developed a collaborative management platform based on high-precision BIM models.
The person in charge said that during the construction process of Chow Taifu, the project department first carried out BIM construction in the virtual world, and then carried out the construction of physical entities after scientific verification, thus eliminating the problems that may have been demolished and reworked in the previous construction project.
In 2017, the BIM innovation achievements of the Chow Tai Fook Financial Center project won the first prize of the global engineering construction industry global excellence award construction team at the global AU Master Hui and the 2017 Global Engineering Construction Industry Global Excellence Award Ceremony.
During the construction of the project, the project department created more than 130 national patent achievements.
It is worth mentioning that the BIM innovation achievements and the promotion of scientific and technological innovation of the Tianjin Chow Taifu Project have not only achieved an advantage in all the complex and extensive construction links, shortened the construction period by more than four months, but also led to a substantial improvement in safety management and other aspects.
Not long ago, the Tianjin Chow Daifu Financial Center project also won the 2019 ISA International Security Award.
The 86th China-Laos Myanmar-Thailand-Mekong River joint patrol law enforcement was completed.
The reporter learned from the press office of the Public Security Department of Yunnan Province on the 27th that at 15:30 on the same day, China's three law enforcement boats and two law enforcement boats and two law enforcement boats in Laos participated in the 86th China-Laos-Thailand-Mekong River joint patrol, marking the successful conclusion of the joint patrol and law enforcement operation.
The operation was launched on the 24th in the port, which lasted 4 days and 3 nights, sending a total of 136 law enforcement personnel and 6 law enforcement boats in the four countries.
During the operation, the formation carried out joint patrols, anti-drug propaganda and other activities in key waters such as the Golden River Delta, the Lao Banshan fruit, and Mengmo.
In addition, the Chinese side also sent a team of police actual combat instructors to the 222 and 133 border companies of the Lao People's Army to carry out the exchange of police practical combat skills, and effectively improved the emergency response capabilities of law enforcement personnel of the two sides to jointly deal with emergencies.
The four countries also held a law enforcement cooperation and exchange meeting in Qingsheng, Thailand, to inform each other about the recent situation of various countries in border management, the fight against drug crimes and the public security situation in the Mekong River basin, and reached a consensus on strengthening information exchange, research and judgment and law enforcement cooperation.
According to the relevant person in charge of the water patrol team of the Public Security Department of Yunnan Province, after the end of the operation, the two sides will also continue to carry out a 10-day joint training and segmented joint patrol task, improve the Mekong River police rate, and make every effort to maintain the safety and stability of the Mekong River Basin.
Thailand's commander-in-chief said that since the launch of the Mekong River joint patrol and law enforcement, China and Laos Myanmar and Thailand have held close exchanges, deepened practical cooperation, and achieved fruitful results in various fields such as law enforcement and security cooperation and cultural exchanges.
It is hoped that the law enforcement cooperation between the four sides will continue to deepen and expand, strive to open up a new situation of law enforcement cooperation between the four countries, and make new contributions to maintaining the security and stability of the Mekong River Basin.
Iran's Defense Minister Amir Khatami said on the 25th that he opposes reaching any agreement with the West on Iran's missile program.
The Islamic Republic News Agency quoted Khatami as saying that any agreement reached with the United States on Iran's "missile force" will damage Iran's capabilities.
According to Khatami, Iran’s leaders all support an improved missile program.
Iran and Iran reached an agreement in 2015, and the United States withdrew from the agreement in May last year and restored and strengthened sanctions against Iran, trying to use extreme pressure to force Iran and the United States to renegotiate the Iranian nuclear agreement to limit Iran's weapons programs and regional activities.
Some Western leaders used the occasion of the United Nations General Assembly to mediate US-Iran tensions.
British Prime Minister Boris Johnson, German Chancellor Angela Merkel and French President Emmanuel Macron met on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly on the 23rd.
After the meeting, the leaders of the three countries issued a joint statement urging Iran to participate in the dialogue on nuclear activities, missile programs and regional security issues.
Iranian President Hassan Rouhani told reporters on the 24th that Iran is willing to discuss "small changes, additions or amendments" to the Iranian nuclear agreement, provided that the United States lifts sanctions.
2019 Tokyo International Film Festival Zhang Ziyi as the head of the jury
As the only Chinese-language film directed by Wang Rui, a professor at the Beijing Film Institute, it was shortlisted for the main competition unit of the 32nd Tokyo International Film Festival, which opened on October 28, and it will compete with 13 other shortlisted films for the highest award of the Tokyo International Film Festival.
"Under the White Cloud" is the fifth film directed by Professor Wang Rui of "Peach Li", which tells the story of an ordinary Mongolian herdsmen husband and wife, a certain life dilemma caused by the different pursuits of life, played by the Mongolian actors Jizimutu and Tana.
It is reported that "Under the White Cloud" held two world premiere events during the film festival, and the release dates were October 31 and November 3 respectively.
The 32nd Tokyo International Film Festival is scheduled from October 28 to November 5 this year, held in Tokyo's Roppongi, Hibiya and other venues, on the afternoon of September 26, the Film Festival Organizing Committee held a press conference, officially announced the main competition for the Golden Kirin Award, "Asia's future" unit, "special hospitality works", Japanese Cinema Splash, "World Focus" and other units, the list of films.
The person in charge of the competition film selection introduced the Chinese participating film "Under the White Cloud".
Zhang Ziyi is the chairman of the international jury of the main competition unit of the film festival.
There are three Chinese-language films in the “Asian Future” unit.
In a series of modules of the Tokyo International Film Festival, its important position is second only to the "Asian Future" unit of the main competition film, although there are only eight shortlisted films, 6 fewer than the main competition, but there are three Chinese-language films from mainland China and Hong Kong.
The two Hong Kong films are "Baby's Revenge" directed by Lu Yixin, and Huang Qingxun's "The Horseman" starring Shadow Emperor Guo Fucheng and Yang Qianzhi after the film. A mainland film is "Summer Night Knight" directed by Yuxing.
In addition, the Sino-Japanese cooperative action adventure film "Ice Peak Storm", directed by Yu Fei and starring Zhang Jingchu and Lin Baihong, will also be released at this film festival as a "special hospitality work".
The spokesperson of the film festival, the "goddess" Alice, was absent from the press conference for any reason and issued a video speech.
The famous director Yamada.
At the press conference, in August this year, the president of the Tokyo International Film Festival, Ando Yukang, the director of the film festival, as well as the heads of selected films of various units, successively delivered speeches, introducing the purpose of the film festival and the release of various films.
As a special guest of the press conference, the opening film, the 50th work of the "Ein Jiro" series, "The Story of Yinjiro: Welcome Returns", director Yamada Yogi, two Japanese film directors who were shortlisted for the main main competition unit, "Balobora"), "Comedy Love Wife Story"), as well as the well-known playwright and screenwriter Nakashima, also appeared at this press conference to talk about the feeling of participating in the Tokyo Film Festival.
The international jury of the main competition unit is composed of 5 people, the chairman of the jury is China's Zhang Ziyi, and the other four are American producer Bill Geber, French actor and producer Julie Garyer, Danish director Michael Noel, and Japanese director Guang Mulongyi.
In addition, TIFFCOM (International Image Market), held in parallel with the Tokyo International Film Festival, will be held from October 22 to 24 at the Ikebukuro Sunshine City Convention and Exhibition Center. This year, there will be a record number of 401 group exhibition booths, especially from 90 exhibitors from China, compared with last year's 14, an increase of 6.4 times.
To this end, TIFFCOM, in particular, designated the opening day on October 22 as "CHINA DAY", held a number of lectures, seminars, etc., and invited Japanese director Ishii Yu also participated in relevant activities, and the welcome dinner on the evening of the day was also co-hosted by China and Japan.
Chengdu's "Panda Planet" and Giant Panda Breeding Research Base Expansion Project Begins
Xinhua News Agency, Chengdu, September 27 (Reporter Li Qianwei) Rich giant panda cultural themed tourist routes, panda base in the future can accommodate 180 giant pandas. "Panda Planet" and giant panda breeding research base expansion project officially started in Chengdu on the 25th, which means that the "Panda Capital" project planned and built in Chengdu was officially launched.
According to the plan, the "panda capital" built in Chengdu is composed of three areas: Beihu District, Dujiangyan District and Longquan Mountain Area, with an area of 69 square kilometers.
It is planned to combine the ecological and cultural values of giant pandas with the urban construction of Chengdu's beautiful livable parks to create an ecological home for giant pandas.
"Panda Planet" belongs to the North Lake area, covers an area of 35 square kilometers, combined with industrial planning, will form "1+N+X" regional spatial structure.
One core attraction is the renovation and expansion project of the giant panda breeding research base; N cultural tourism consumption scenarios are created, that is, panda town, remote park, dream garden, etc.; X regional basic supporting facilities.
After the renovation and expansion of the giant panda breeding research base in Chengdu, the scale will reach 3,525 acres, which will be positioned as a world-class giant panda protection demonstration place, and people and animals have a good time to share.
The park is planned to accommodate 180 giant pandas and their accompanying animals (little pandas and golden monkeys).
According to the "News and Newspaper Abstracts" of the Central Radio and Television Station, in the past few days, a number of international dignitaries and envoys of various countries have congratulated on the 70th anniversary of the founding of New China, highly appreciating the development achievements of New China and its significance for global development.
In an interview with reporters from the Central Radio and Television Station, President Keita of Mali said that he has visited China many times, and China's development achievements in the past 70 years have been amazing and benefited the world.
Keita: I am the friend and sincere friend of the Chinese people.
China has never developed selfishly, but has opened its doors to the world and brought the greatest happiness to the peoples of the world.
We hope that China will succeed in everything, and I hope that President Xi Jinping will lead the great Chinese people to continue to realize their dreams.
Happy Birthday and Blessings to China!
The Prime Minister of Barbados, Mottley, said he wished the People's Republic of China a happy birthday.
Greetings to the Chinese people.
I’ll never forget it, because it’s also my birthday.
A few days ago (25th), envoys from more than 130 countries and representatives of international organizations in China visited the "Great History and Brilliant Achievements - Celebrating the 70th Anniversary of the Founding of the People's Republic of China".
Russia's Ambassador to China Denisov said: personally see the starting point of China's reform and opening up policy, compared with today and more than 40 years ago, the progress is too great.
In addition, in recent days, our embassies and consulates in many countries have also held a variety of activities to celebrate the 70th anniversary of the founding of New China with local friendly people.
Many foreign friends have sent heartfelt blessings to China.
On September 26, Baidu announced that it would launch the trial operation of Robotaxi, a fully self-driving taxi team, on a specific highway in Changsha City, Hunan Province.
The self-driving start-up Pony Zhihang has also launched trial operations in Guangzhou, Guangdong Province.
The pilot operation of self-driving taxis supported by the Chinese government may be expanded everywhere.
Since the 26th, Baidu has used 45 self-driving taxis for trial operation, and passengers in Changsha City can apply for a ride through a special website.
There are "safety officers" in the driver's seat to ensure the safety of passengers.
The road providing trial operation is 50 kilometers by the end of 2019, and it is planned to be extended to 135 kilometers by the first half of 2020.
The vehicle is the "red flag EV" of China FAW Group's pure electric vehicle, equipped with the system developed by Baidu's "Apollo Project", which was established and supported by the Chinese government.
Baidu's Apollo program, in addition to Toyota and Honda, there are more than 150 companies such as German Volkswagen, Germany's Daimler, U.S.-based Ford, U.S. Intel, U.S. Microsoft and U.S. Nvidia.
Around China's self-driving taxis, China's largest online ride-hailing service provider Didi Chuxu released a plan to launch 30 self-driving taxi services on the outskirts of Shanghai this year.
China's self-driving development competition may become more intense.
Taiwanese scholars advise: "Uncertain years" Taiwanese businessmen need to keep up with the development of mainstream industries in the mainland
The "2019 Taiwan Business Innovation Business Model Forum" was held in Taipei for two consecutive days on the 26th and 27th.
The event invited a number of Taiwanese business representatives and scholars to share their experiences on enterprise transformation, innovation, succession and market development.
The forum was organized by the Taipei Business Management Research Institute and co-organized by Qunyi Jinding Securities and the Outstanding Continental Taiwan Business Association.
The two-day meeting was divided into a number of seminars such as the transformation and upgrading model and business strategy, and more than 100 people attended the meeting.
Chen Mingzhang, president of the Taipei Business Management Research Institute, said that trade frictions between the United States and China (mainland China) continued, and Taiwanese businessmen faced an "uncertain era."
He believes that Taiwanese businesses need to keep pace with the times and keep up with the mainstream industries developed by the mainland, paying special attention to innovative products related to the fields of science and technology, culture, tourism and health.
â€œIn the past, Taiwanese businessmen paid attention to quality, effectiveness and delivery.â€
Chen Mingzhang believes that only the above-mentioned conditions are not enough.
He pointed out that Taiwan-funded enterprises should have both speed and services, accelerate the speed of the supply chain, and pay attention to extended services and life products and services.
In addition, "service value-added" is also a new field that Taiwanese companies can vigorously develop.
During the speech, Xu Wentang, chairman of Taiwan Merchants Electronics Co., Ltd. from Guangdong Province, said that Yami Electronics had caused operational difficulties due to a sharp decline in orders, and the Group began to improve its business from various aspects such as structural adjustment and reactivation of assets.
Removing the traditional electrical appliance business, transforming vehicle electronic equipment, and entering the smart home appliance industry, it took three years for the company to achieve revenue.
Bai Hongzhang, general manager of Sun God (Zhuhai) Electronics Co., Ltd., proposed that if it is difficult to develop new customers, it is better to focus on the "one-stop" service provided by original customers.
The customer replaces the six factors of poor service, high price, low quality, slow delivery speed, few varieties, and integrity problems, as long as these six points are solved, coupled with the timely transformation of the production line and the expansion of the product category, the company will become an irreplaceable supplier for customers.
On the 27th, the award ceremony of "2019 Outstanding Mainland Taiwan Business Award" also sponsored by the Taipei Management Research Institute was held in Taipei.
According to Taiwan's "Economic Daily" reported that the general manager of the operation center in Shanghai's Golden Land Company Lv Zhengzhang won the "outstanding Taiwanese business and cross-strait contribution award".
The new regulations for comments: social capital needs to be qualified to obtain rural land management rights
Social capital needs to be qualified to obtain rural land management rights.
"Rural land management rights transfer management measures" for public consultation to control the transfer of social capital such as industrial and commercial enterprises to obtain land management rights
Yesterday, the website of the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs issued a notice on the "Administrative Measures for the Transfer of Rural Land Management Rights (Revised Draft)" (hereinafter referred to as the "Draft Opinions"), which increased the supervision and risk prevention of the transfer of social capital from industrial and commercial enterprises to obtain land management rights.
From now on, the draft opinion will be publicly solicited from the public.
According to the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, in order to implement the newly revised "Rural Land Contracting Law", further consolidate and improve the basic rural management system, deepen the reform of the rural land system, and implement the "three rights separation" system, the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs has revised the "Measures for the Management of the Transfer of Rural Land Contracting Rights" and formed the Draft Opinions.
The Beijing Youth Daily reporter learned that there are many important amendments to the "Draft of Opinions" released for the first time.
The newly revised "rural land contracting law" clarifies the scope of land transfer, implements the concept of "separation of powers", and sets up "land contracting management rights" and "land management rights" respectively, making a clear distinction between the transfer of land contractual management rights, swaps and the transfer of land management rights (leasing, subcontracting, shareholding, or other methods).
In the "Draft of Opinions", in order to implement the concept of "separation of powers", effectively respond to the "rural land contracting law" to amend the essence of the law, taking into account that there is a big difference between the transfer of land management rights and the exchange of land contractual management rights, the transfer of the transfer of parties, procedures, supervision and other aspects, this revised draft defines the scope of transfer, focusing on the transfer of land management rights, transfer methods, etc.
For the transfer and exchange of land contractual management rights, administrative measures will be issued separately.
According to the "Draft of Opinions", in the context of the "separation of powers", farmers' shareholding is only a certain period of land management rights.
In theory, even in the event of bankruptcy liquidation, farmers only have the risk of losing a certain period of business rights, so it is no longer necessary to legally return to the original contractor of the contracting place, and there is a conflict with the bankruptcy law.
In response to the problem of preventing the risk of land loss for farmers, in practice, preferred stocks, first rent after shares, repurchases and other methods have been generated.
Taking into account that preferred stocks have a more mature theoretical discussion in corporate law, it is recommended to use it as an advocacy provision to prevent the risk of losing shares.
